# WoW-style controls specification (camera ↔ character ↔ input)

Canonical behaviour for **`ThirdPersonOrbitCamera`**, **`KeyboardInputSource`**, **`PlayerMovement`**, and **`TargetingController`**.

When fixing bugs, resolve conflicts in favour of this document and the implementations it names — do not silently change UX without deciding here first.

---

## Execution order (why timing matters)

- **`ThirdPersonOrbitCamera`**: `LateUpdate`, `[DefaultExecutionOrder(-50)]` — applies mouse deltas, orbit offset, **`MouseMode`**, **`Yaw`**, drag (**`IsLmbDragging`**), **`ManageCursor`**. With default order **`0`** on **`PlayerMovement`**, runs **before** that script’s **`LateUpdate`** each frame so **`Yaw`** / **`MouseMode`** are stable for visuals.
- **`KeyboardInputSource`**: **`Update`** — reads **`ThirdPersonOrbitCamera.Yaw`** and derives **`AlwaysFaceYaw`**, **`MoveAxes`** (both-buttons auto-forward, etc.).
- **`FusionInputProvider.OnInput`** — samples **`IInputSource`** once per Fusion tick (`MoveAxes`, **`LookYaw`**, **`AlwaysFaceYaw`**, buttons).
- **`PlayerMovement`**: **`FixedUpdateNetwork`** (state authority only) — **`CharacterController.Move`**, planar facing from **`GameplayInput`**.
- **`PlayerMovement`** also uses **`LateUpdate`** on the **local input authority**: applies visual rotation from **`ThirdPersonOrbitCamera.Yaw`** when RMB/strafe/key rules require instant feedback between ticks (`AlwaysFaceYaw` / mouse mode mirrored from **`KeyboardInputSource`** + **`MouseMode`**).
- **`TargetingController`**: **`Update`** — LMB release runs **before** the camera clears **`IsLmbDragging`** in **`LateUpdate`**, so a click vs orbit-drag is read correctly **the same frame**.

---

## Mouse: camera yaw vs orbit offset

The camera exposes **`Yaw`** = character-facing yaw (**`_charYaw`**). LMB-only orbit adds **`_orbitOffset`** so horizontal mouse moves rotate the lens **without** rotating the character (**`Yaw`** unchanged by LMB deltas).

On **first RMB press this hold**, **`_orbitOffset`** is folded into **`_charYaw`** and reset so the avatar snaps to where the lens was pointing (WoW RMB pickup).

Horizontal mouse deltas while **either** LMB or RMB is held tilt pitch and apply yaw either to **`_orbitOffset`** (LMB only) or **`_charYaw`** (RMB or both).

---

## Mouse modes (`CameraMouseMode`)

| Held | Rotation | **`AlwaysFaceYaw` context** (see Keyboard) |
|------|-----------|--------------------------------------------|
| None | Keyboard Q/E/arrows rotate **`Yaw`** via **`AddYaw`**. Mouse alone does nothing. | Off unless keys/strafe (below). |
| **LMB only** | Orbit: **`_orbitOffset`** from mouse **`_charYaw`** unchanged **by LMB**. | Typically off when only LMB (**see strafe exception**). |
| **RMB only** | Free-look: **`_charYaw`** from mouse. | **On** → move/facing tied to **`LookYaw`**. |
| **Both** | Same rotation as **RMB**; **`KeyboardInputSource`** forces forward movement (auto-run). | **On**. |

Scroll wheel adjusts orbit distance clamped **[ `_minDistance`, `_maxDistance` ]**.

Serialized drag threshold (**`_dragThresholdPixels`**, default ~**20**) is accumulated **per button press** using **`delta.magnitude`** (LMB tracked for targeting; **`IsRmbDragging`** is tracked internally but **not** used for the cursor gate below).

---

## Cursor lock / visibility (**`ThirdPersonOrbitCamera.ManageCursor`**)

Implementations MUST match:

- **RMB held** (includes **both** buttons): cursor **locked + hidden immediately**, even when the mouse is still.
- **LMB held**: cursor stays **visible and unlocked** until **`IsLmbDragging`** becomes true (**accumulated** LMB drag &gt; threshold this press). After that it stays locked while LMB remains held (even if the mouse stops), so orbit feels like RMB once drag has begun.
- **Neither** LMB nor **RMB** requires lock (`ManageCursor(false)` branch): **`Cursor.lockState = None`**, **`visible = true`**.

**Targeting depends on LMB leaving the cursor free until orbit-drag is acknowledged** — **`TargetingController`** raycasts **`Mouse.current.position`** on LMB **release** when **`!IsLmbDragging`**. Do **not** lock on bare LMB press.

