## Keyboard (`KeyboardInputSource`)

| Input | Behaviour |
|-------|-----------|
| **W / S / Up / Down** | Forward / back (**Y** axis of **`MoveAxes`**). |
| **A / D** | Strafe (**X**). |
| **Q / E / ← / →** | Rotate camera: **`ThirdPersonOrbitCamera.AddYaw`**, unless **LMB-only** mode then **`AddCharYawKeepCamera`** (turn body, keep lens world-angle). |
| **Both LMB+RMB** | **`MoveAxes.y`** clamped so forward is applied (effectively press **W** as well). |
| **Space**, **1/2/3**, **R** | Edge-triggered consumes for jump / spells / colour (see **`FusionInputProvider`**). |

**`AlwaysFaceYaw`** is **`true`** when **any** of: **RMB** or **Both** mouse modes; **Q/E/arrows** held; **A/D** strafe active (**so strafes keep body aligned with **`LookYaw`**, WoW-like**). It is **`false`** for **pure LMB orbit** without strafe/Q/E/arrows/RMB — then movement-facing uses **character forward** (**`FixedUpdateNetwork`**) instead of **`LookYaw`**.

**`LookYaw`** written each **`Update`** = **`ThirdPersonOrbitCamera.Yaw`**.

---

## Character controller (**`PlayerMovement`**)

Runs only with **state authority** and alive, non-casting (when **`NetworkCombatController.IsCasting`**).

- Builds planar move vector from **`GameplayInput.Move`**.
- **`AlwaysFaceYaw` set →** move relative to **`LookYaw`** quaternion; **clear →** relative to planar **character forward**.
- Applies jump edge + gravity · **`CharacterController.Move`** inside **`Runner.DeltaTime`**.
- **`AlwaysFaceYaw` set →** **`transform.forward`** aligns to **`LookYaw`** in **ticks** as well (**`LateUpdate`** on owner smooths/strafes+RMB visually).

Changing this contract requires checking **orbit strafe**, **RMB pickups**, **LMB orbit without body snap**, and **cursor + click targeting**.

---

## Target selection (local)

| Action | Result |
|--------|--------|
| **Tab** | Cycle alive **`Targetable`**, skip local player. |
| **LMB** release **without** drag (**`!IsLmbDragging`**) | Raypick from cursor through **`Camera.main`**; Fusion **`PhysicsScene`** first, **`Physics`** fallback — select **`Targetable`** or leave selection unchanged if miss/non-target (**WoW-ish**). |
| **Escape** | Clear selection. |

**Drag rule**: LMB movement **beyond** **`_dragThresholdPixels`** ⇒ **`IsLmbDragging`**; release does **not** fire the picker.

